  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "As Udon catches on and more people start using it, people will want to be able to localize their worlds, this includes such things as printing dates differently, offering a language select, or even getting the primary language of the user.\nAs it is currently, operations as simple as printing out the date, or a schedule for an event are difficult to do with no way to specify a region format to stick with, since the exposed ToString() method will only print out in the system language unless presented with an alternate locale, which we do not have the available methods to retrieve, as dates printed in an American format with swedish words for the month and day of the week will be quite awkward.\nhttps://docs.microsoft.com/en-us/dotnet/api/system.globalization.cultureinfo?view=netframework-4.8\nThis request is for all the functions and properties required to at least look up a locale if not to get the system locale so any Udon world can be localized.  They are listed below:\nProperties:\nDateTimeFormat\nEnglishName\nNativeName\nName\nNumberFormat\nFunctions:\nGetCultureInfo\nGetFormat\nOptional Properties:\nCurrentCulture\nCurrentUICulture\nInstalledUICulture\nUseUserOverride",
